{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Commit to keeping electronic training collars legal in England",
        "additional_details": "Protecting dogs, livestock, wildlife and the public requires practical training options. We believe a blanket ban could leave some owners with fewer effective ways to address dangerous chasing and other serious behaviours. Policy should consider each dog\u2019s needs, the evidence on welfare and the consequences of removing an option. We ask the Government to uphold existing protections against cruelty and commit to keeping responsible electronic-collar use lawful in England.",
        "background": "Commit not to ban the use of electronic training collars in England, including remote-controlled static-pulse collars for dogs. Preserve owners\u2019 and trainers\u2019 ability to use them lawfully, subject to the Animal Welfare Act 2006.",
